<article class="env-remark" id="0DU8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DU8">Remark <span data-tag="0DU8">101.45.2</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. Let $U \to \mathcal{X}$ be a morphism whose source is an algebraic space. Let $G \to H$ be the pullback of the morphism $\mathcal{I}_\mathcal {X} \to \mathcal{X} \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{I}_\mathcal {Y}$ to $U$. If $\Delta _ f$ is unramified, étale, etc, so is $G \to H$. This is true because </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ U \times _\mathcal {X} U \ar[r] \ar[d] &  \mathcal{X} \ar[d]^{\Delta _ f} \\  U \times _\mathcal {Y} U \ar[r] &  \mathcal{X} \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{X} }  \]
</div>
  <p> is cartesian and the morphism $G \to H$ is the base change of the left vertical arrow by the diagonal $U \to U \times U$. Compare with the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0CPL" data-tag="0CPL">101.6.6</a>. </p>
</article>